TITLE      Differential cross-section for the T(12C,T)12C         S0233  1    3 
           elastic recoil reaction                                S0233  1    4 
AUTHOR     (Yiming Duan,Wei Ding,Weidu Wang,Wei Zhang,Liqun Shi)  S0233  1    5 
INSTITUTE  (3CPRFUD,3CPRNPC)                                      S0233  1    6 
REFERENCE  (J,NIM/B,483,1,2020)                                   S0233  1    7 
           #doi:10.1016/j.nimb.2020.10.001                        S0233  1    8 
FACILITY   (VDGT,3CPRFUD) NEC 9SDH-2 2x3 MV tandem accelerator    S0233  1    9 
INC-SOURCE The incident beam current was limited to less than 30  S0233  1   10 
           nA as monitored by a Faraday cup. During the           S0233  1   11 
           experiment, the chamber was kept at a high vacuum of   S0233  1   12 
           less than 3.0E-5 Pa.                                   S0233  1   13 
SAMPLE     A thin solid target Ni/TiTx/Al2O3 was prepared by the  S0233  1   14 
           conventional hydrogenation method, the atomic ratios   S0233  1   15 
           of Ti, T and H is 10:8:1, and the atomic thickness of  S0233  1   16 
           the TiTx layer is about 3.5E17 atoms/cm2.              S0233  1   17 
DETECTOR   (SIBAR) An Au/Si surface barrier detector was          S0233  1   18 
           employed to detect the backscattered ions at a         S0233  1   19 
           laboratory angle of 165 deg, with a solid angle of     S0233  1   20 
           0.00183 sr. At a laboratory angle of 30 deg, another   S0233  1   21 
           Au/Si surface barrier detector with a solid angle of   S0233  1   22 
           0.00246 sr was placed to detect the elastic recoil     S0233  1   23 
           spectrum. The angular resolution of both detectors     S0233  1   24 
           were approximately +-0.5 deg and the energy            S0233  1   25 
           resolution of the detection system was about 30 keV    S0233  1   26 
           for 12C ions.                                          S0233  1   27 
METHOD     The relative determination method.                     S0233  1   28 
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) The total error, 5.8%                          S0233  1   29 
           (ERR-1,2.,3.) The error of peak areas resulting from   S0233  1   30 
           the statistics and background, 2-3%                    S0233  1   31 
           (ERR-2)The error of Rutherford scattering cross        S0233  1   32 
           section for Ni-C(E0), 0.44%                            S0233  1   33 
           (ERR-3)The error of Rutherford scattering cross        S0233  1   34 
           section for T-O(ER), 2.6%                              S0233  1   35 
           (ERR-4)The error of Rutherford scattering cross        S0233  1   36 
           section for Ni-O(ER0), 0.53%                           S0233  1   37 
